# Export these in the shell/service environment. This example is NOT auto-loaded.
FOCUS_WORKSPACE=/absolute/path/to/reading-workspace
FOCUS_HOST_DATA=/absolute/path/to/focus-host-data

# Which Agent runtime serves reading turns. The UI, the Reader contract and Core
# are identical either way; switching later starts a new conversation.
# codex     -> pinned Codex App Server 0.154.0 (install host/requirements.txt)
# workbuddy -> unavailable until domestic Open Platform integration is implemented
# FOCUS_BACKEND=codex

# --- codex backend -----------------------------------------------------------
# Omit to use the configured Codex model. No guessed/default model ID is imposed.
# FOCUS_CODEX_MODEL=your-account-supported-model
# Optional: reuse the Host user's existing Codex sign-in, or configure API auth:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-locally
# Optional pinned executable instead of the bundled one; must be exactly 0.154.0.
# FOCUS_CODEX_BIN=/absolute/path/to/codex.exe

# --- domestic WorkBuddy ------------------------------------------------------
# Not connected yet. Requires a WorkBuddy Open Platform application and OAuth.
# See docs/FOCUS_WorkBuddy_Local_Setup.md. CODEBUDDY_API_KEY/CLI login are not substitutes.
# No WorkBuddy credential configuration is consumed by Host yet.

# Codex subprocess-only routing: inherit (default), bypass, or a proxy URL.
# FOCUS_CODEX_PROXY=inherit

# --- shared ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parser calls need this (or a .env in Workspace, per existing parser behavior):
# MINERU_API_TOKEN=replace-locally
# Optional persistent web access token; omitted => random token printed on startup.
# FOCUS_HOST_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-value
# Only for an explicitly configured private server/reverse proxy:
# FOCUS_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://focus.example.com
